// ================= Page 2 =================
== Carry across the candidate set
Mexico's 2s10s steepener is the best-paid trade per unit of risk (#n.mx_carry bp/3m on #n.mx_vol bp vol, ratio #n.mx_cv), but it enters #n.mx_z $sigma$ steep to its 5y history with #n.mx_path12 bp of hikes already in the forwards, so its carry and its mean-reversion point in opposite directions. Brazil's ratio is smaller (#n.br_cv) and its signals agree. A cross-market check isolates the local story: BR minus US 5s10s sits at #n.box_level bp (z #n.box_z) and the two slopes' daily changes are uncorrelated (#n.box_corr), so Brazil's flatness is not imported global duration, it is local pricing.

#figure(image("/output/figs/fig_carry_per_vol.pdf", width: 86%),
  caption: [MX pays most per unit of risk but against a #n.mx_z $sigma$-steep slope; BR's smaller ratio buys a trade whose carry and z-score agree.])

