[
  == What kills it
  - *Flattening to the exit.* A move to #n.br_inval bp (#n.kill_move bp) erases #n.kill_quarters quarters of carry; I exit there rather than average.
  - *The realized tail.* The worst 3m flattening of the past 5y is #n.kill_worst3m bp (#n.kill_worst3m_when). A repeat swamps the #n.br_carry bp quarterly carry, this is a repricing trade, not a carry trade.
  - *Measurement.* My curve is retail (Tesouro Direto): #n.rb_5y bp vs interbank at 5y, #n.rb_10y bp at 10y. The #n.rb_5s10s bp differential biases the slope; a widening beyond the quarterly carry dominates measured P&L.
],
[
  == Catalysts
  #owner[
    - Copom communication that opens the door to easing; the front reprices first, the 5y follows hardest. #text(fill: accent, size: 8pt)[[your read on timing]]
    - Inflation prints versus target that validate the real-rate cushion at #n.br_policy% policy. #text(fill: accent, size: 8pt)[[your numbers]]
    - Fiscal news steepens the 10y independently: helps the trade, but for the wrong reason; I take profit, not add.
  ]
